Machine Learning Tools 🧠

Navigation nodes, these control which ML sections appear in SageMaker Studio.

💻 Compute

| Tool                                    | Purpose                                  |
| --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| **Compute**                             | Manage computing resources               |
| **HyperPod clusters**                   | Large-scale AI/ML cluster infrastructure |
| **Resilient clusters for ML workloads** | Reliable compute for ML tasks            |


=====

📊 Data

| Tool              | Purpose                                                |
| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| **Data Wrangler** | Clean, prepare, and transform data                     |
| **Feature Store** | Store and manage ML features                           |
| **EMR clusters**  | Process large-scale data using big-data infrastructure |
====
Example:

Raw Data 📂
    ↓
Data Wrangler 🧹
    ↓
Clean Data 📊
    ↓
Feature Store
    ↓
ML Model 🧠

=====

🤖 AutoML

AutoML helps automate parts of machine learning, such as model selection and training.

Instead of manually trying many models:

Your Data
   ↓
AutoML 🤖
   ↓
Tries models automatically
   ↓
Finds a suitable model

=====

🧪 Experiments

Used to track different ML experiments.

Example:

Experiment 1 → Random Forest → 85%
Experiment 2 → XGBoost → 91%
Experiment 3 → Neural Network → 94%

This helps compare which experiment performs best.

=====

💼 Jobs

This section manages different ML jobs:

| Tool                       | Purpose                             |
| -------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| **Training jobs**          | Train ML models                     |
| **Model evaluations**      | Evaluate model performance          |
| **Inference optimization** | Improve prediction performance/cost |
| **Performance evaluation** | Check model efficiency              |


=====

🏗️ Pipelines

A Pipeline automates the ML workflow:

Data
 ↓
Data Processing
 ↓
Training
 ↓
Evaluation
 ↓
Deployment

====

Instead of running each step manually, the pipeline manages the workflow.

====

🧠 Models

This is where trained ML models are managed.

Example:

Training Job
     ↓
Trained Model 🧠
     ↓
Save / Register
     ↓
Deploy

====

🚀 JumpStart

SageMaker JumpStart provides ready-to-use:

Foundation models
ML models
Solution templates

For example, you can start with an existing AI model instead of building everything from scratch.

====

🌐 Deployments

After training a model, you need to make it available for predictions.

Trained Model 🧠
      ↓
Deployment 🚀
      ↓
API Endpoint
      ↓
Website / App
      ↓
Prediction

====

options like:

Inference recommender → Helps select suitable deployment resources.
Inference optimization → Helps improve inference performance.


